  "nl_text": "This database schema, named rschema_0478, is used to store information about a bicycle-sharing system. It consists of five tables: user, bicycle, trip_record, fault_record, and billing_rule.\nThe user table contains information about the users of the bicycle-sharing system, including their ID, phone number, name, credit, and status. The bicycle table contains information about the bicycles themselves, including their ID, location, status, and unlock code.\nThe trip_record table contains information about each trip taken by a user, including the user's ID, bicycle ID, start and end times, cost, payment status, and rule ID. The trip_record table also has foreign key constraints that reference the bicycle and user tables.\nThe fault_record table contains information about any faults or issues that occur with the bicycles, including the user's ID, bicycle ID, reporting time, and fault description. The fault_record table also has foreign key constraints that reference the bicycle and user tables.\nThe billing_rule table contains information about the billing rules for the bicycle-sharing system, including the rule ID, billing method, unit price, and minimum fee.\nOverall, this schema is designed to store and manage information about a bicycle-sharing system, including users, bicycles, trips, faults, and billing rules. The schema is well-structured and has appropriate foreign key constraints to ensure data integrity and consistency.",
  "gold_question": "Business Requirements Description for the Shared Bicycle Management System:\nThe shared bicycle company manages multiple users, each with a user ID, phone number, name, credit, and status.\nThe company manages multiple bicycles, each with a bicycle ID, location, status, and unlock code.\nThe company records multiple trips, each trip requiring the recording of user and bicycle usage information, including bicycle number, start time, end time, cost, and payment status.\nThe company manages multiple fault records, each fault involving the user number who encountered the fault, bicycle number, fault description, and reporting time.\nThe company also manages billing rules, each rule including the billing method, unit price, and minimum fee.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0478.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0478\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `phone_number` varchar(15) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `credit` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0.00,\n  `status` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `bicycle` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `unlock_code` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `trip_record` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `bicycle_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `start_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `end_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `cost` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `payment_status` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `rule_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `trip_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `trip_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`bicycle_id`) REFERENCES `bicycle` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `fault_record` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `bicycle_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `reporting_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `fault_description` text NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `fault_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `fault_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`bicycle_id`) REFERENCES `bicycle` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `billing_rule` (\n  `rule_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `billing_method` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `unit_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `minimum_fee` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`rule_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
